# =============================================================================
# CardDemo — Frontend build-context exclusions (Docker).
#
# This file trims the `./frontend` build context that `frontend/Dockerfile`
# copies (the deps stage copies `package.json`/`package-lock.json`; the builder
# stage copies the rest with `COPY . .`). Everything matched here is NEVER sent
# to the Docker daemon and therefore can never land in an image layer. It
# resolves QA finding M-26:
#
#   * Image bloat + broken inputs: without exclusions, `COPY . .` sent a
#     ~996.94 MB context that baked the host `node_modules/` and the already-
#     built `.next/` output into the image. Both are regenerated inside the
#     build (`node_modules` comes from the deps stage via `COPY --from=deps`;
#     `.next` is produced by `next build`), so neither belongs in the context.
#   * Latent secret-in-image: the documented dev workflow copies
#     `.env.local.example` to `.env.local` (a real local secret file that is
#     present in this directory). Excluding every `.env*` file structurally
#     guarantees a runtime secret can never be copied into an image layer (Ochs
#     Rule #3 — secrets come from the runtime environment; only NEXT_PUBLIC_*
#     build args, which are public by design, are baked in).
#
# Build-required inputs are intentionally NOT excluded: `package.json`,
# `package-lock.json`, `src/`, `next.config.js`, `tsconfig.json`, and
# `next-env.d.ts` all remain in the context.
# =============================================================================

# --- Installed dependencies (resolved fresh in the deps stage; broken host ABI)
node_modules/

# --- Next.js build output and static export (regenerated by `next build`)
.next/
out/

# --- Test suite and coverage (not part of the runtime image; excluding it also
#     stops `next build` from type-checking test files that pull dev-only types)
__tests__/
coverage/

# --- TypeScript / tool caches and incremental build info (regenerated)
*.tsbuildinfo
.swc/
.eslintcache

# --- Secret / environment files (never bake a secret into the image).
#     `.env.local.example` is intentionally excluded too — the image needs no
#     template; NEXT_PUBLIC_* configuration is supplied as a build arg instead.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# --- Package-manager debug logs (never runtime inputs)
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Version control and Docker meta (the image needs neither)
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# --- OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Logs and ad-hoc validation scratch files
*.log
blitzy_adhoc_test_*
